+## Bounded Development Readiness
+
+This finite V2.7 candidate governance amendment becomes effective only after its independent acceptance, recorded in the [iteration20 result](../../../template/codex/executions/v2.7-ws06a/iteration20/result.md). Method authority remains this SOP; the [evolution roadmap](../../../template/roadmap/GAME_SITE_SYSTEM_V2.7_EVOLUTION_ROADMAP_V1.md) holds workstream dependencies. Historical design proposals/evidence are preserved inputs, not a second Contract. The amendment defines a development entrance; it does not grant current-source readiness.
+
+Full WS-06A acceptance continues through the existing strict raw qualification or accepted separate closure policy, required real-browser evidence and independent review. Strict `check:browser`, CI and closure validation do not change. Bounded Development Readiness instead supports one candidate WS-03 slice under unresolved Safari evidence. It never closes WS-06A or supplies capability PASS, EXCEPTION, NOT_APPLICABLE, NOT_SELECTED, WAIVED or a non-null verifiedOutcome. P0/P1 requirements, applicability, severity, human review and release obligations remain unchanged.
+
+`WS06A_DEVELOPMENT_READINESS` is a governance workflow record with NOT_EVALUATED, BLOCKED, ACCEPTED_FOR_BOUNDED_DEVELOPMENT or STALE, not a Registry field, Contract ID, §W outcome or production schema. Governance acceptance activates this method only. Current readiness is NOT_EVALUATED; WS-06A remains BLOCKED, Safari proof0, and no WS-03 code has started. Eight workstreams and41 capability IDs remain unchanged; this amendment closes no additional workstream.
+
+### Current-source audit and exact residual evidence
+
+After governance acceptance, independently audit the current source before signing a finite readiness record. Execute all47 unchanged planned cases and required assertions, no skip/NOT_RUN/missing row; require every non-WebKit row/assertion PASS, repaired live-resize PASS and zero unknown infrastructure failures. Preserve actual raw FAIL and command exit; development eligibility is a separate reviewer decision, not a browser command PASS.
+
+Use the independently accepted exact residual evidence as frozen comparison input. The historical initial input is10 WebKit failed rows/40 assertions:37 ENVIRONMENT_PROFILE_BLOCKED and3 PRODUCT_EVIDENCE_UNRESOLVED, with80 dual-engine PASS counterparts. These counts describe evidence, not a permanent product standard. Failure identity includes caseId/category/role/route/CSS viewport/JavaScript/motion/assertion/disposition; current raw details and native/control evidence must still satisfy the exact applicable policy. Later failed sets may only be subsets. New locations or assertions STOP even if total failures decrease; same-name assertions or similar Tab issues cannot be added automatically. Residual evidence is not a PASS allowlist.
+
+Each remaining residual requires a current Chromium row+assertion PASS and Firefox row+assertion PASS at the same category/role/route/viewport/JS/motion/assertion, with no duplicate or missing match. This is cross-engine corroboration, not Safari proof, WebKit equivalence or majority-vote PASS. Historical counts, old builds and synthetic unit positives do not establish a fresh run.
+
+Bind exact SOP/Prompt/Starter identities and changes; Starter branch/HEAD/working-tree manifest; canonical Contract SHA; matrix/runner/closure verifier SHA; policy/control/raw/native/independently captured expected identity SHA; fixture source/final-dist SHA; Playwright version; all3 engine versions/revisions; host/platform/arch; collection/review dates; reviewer; next slice; expiry and review triggers. Raw self-reported identity alone is not an independent oracle. Related source/config/fixture/dist/verification/tool/host changes make readiness STALE; governance changes require comparability review, not inherited signature. A readiness decision is valid only for its named next slice and cannot authorize all WS-03 work indefinitely.
+
+### One-slice continuation
+
+Require WS-02 acceptance, independently accepted governance and independently accepted current-source readiness before the first finite WS-03 candidate. First scope is WS-03 only:03A,03B,03C,03D-search,03D-freshness one at a time;03C still requires independently accepted actual03B interface input, and03D parts remain separate. No guessed API or evidence-free migration default is approved.
+
+For every slice, record changed files/capabilities, exact pre/post source, interface/compatibility/migration decisions and build output. Source mutation makes old readiness STALE. Run meaningful targeted positive/negative checks first, then root `npm run check`, actual default-final rejection and adopted validate/check/build gates, fresh unchanged47, and additional slice-specific rendered/browser evidence. Theme/state/readability, media valid/missing/failure/no-media/video equivalent/fallback, generated share output, search states and freshness/date semantics need their own applicable evidence; base47 regression does not prove new capability surfaces. Record real per-engine results; new-surface failure cannot enter the old residual set.
+
+Require no non-WebKit regression, exact residual subset with valid current policy/control, complete current dual-engine PASS counterparts, no unknown failure, exact source/build identities, normal preview stop with independent PID-gone confirmation and deletion of only the owned fixture. Missing evidence, new failure, weakened assertion, changed matrix/runner, fake key/focus/scroll, modifier/preference workaround, identity mismatch or cleanup failure blocks continuation. Keep failed runs. Independent `IMPLEMENTATION_ACCEPTED_FOR_CONTINUATION` may authorize only a named next candidate slice; it is not formal WS-03 ACCEPT or capability promotion. See [QA](QA_CHECKLIST.md#bounded-development-readiness-audit) and [execution order](EXECUTION_PROMPT.md#bounded-development-readiness-execution).
+
+### Release hold and reconciliation
+
+Development readiness cannot unlock the WS-03 formal Gate,04A contract/integration,05,04B,06B implementation/acceptance,07,08 or release. While Safari evidence is missing and full06A remains blocked, AX-01/02/03 andPA-01 are not promoted; visual focus/contrast needs separate human review. Development acceptance grants no commit/push/tag/merge/deployment/release action and cannot bypass tool access denial. Commercial representative Safari checks remain required even if the strict raw47 branch later passes.
+
+When source stabilizes: freeze exact current source/build → fresh47 and new surfaces → validate current policy/control → obtain genuine current Safari evidence through an allowed trusted channel → run the actual `verify:browser-closure` → independent full06A review → reconcile every provisional slice against current interfaces/source and rerun stale evidence → independently restore formal WS-03 decisions and the original formal DAG. The existing closure command determines eligibility only, not acceptance. Genuine Safari FAIL keeps06A BLOCKED, requires product repair, makes impacted slice evidence STALE and requires fresh regression/reproof. Engineering investment never waives P0/P1 or the remaining REF, real-adoption, rights, visual and release gates.
 
